{"step_index":53,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-08T07:11:26Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-08T12:41:26+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-08T12:41:27+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/builtin/skills/generative_ui/SKILL.md`\nTotal Lines: 122\nTotal Bytes: 5650\nShowing lines 1 to 122\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: ---\n2: name: generative_ui\n3: description: How to render rich interactive HTML widgets inline in the chat or as standalone artifacts. Use this skill when you want to show the user diagrams, data visualizations, interactive controls, educational walkthroughs, or any rich visual content beyond plain text and markdown.\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # Generative UI\n7: \n8: You can render custom, rich, interactive user interfaces (inline widgets or\n9: larger artifacts) directly in the chat. This is a great way to communicate\n10: complex information to the user, generate rich visualizations, and even create\n11: small interactive experiences for the user.\n12: \n13: ## Workflow\n14: \n15: 1.  **Create the HTML Artifact**: Use `write_to_file` to save a self-contained\n16:     `.html` file (using Tailwind CSS and inline JavaScript) to the artifact\n17:     directory. Set `UserFacing: true` in `ArtifactMetadata`.\n18: 2.  **Embed Inline (optional)**: Include the `<agent-embed>` tag in your chat\n19:     response, if you decide this html artifact should be rendered inline in the\n20:     conversation:\n21: \n22:     ```\n23:     <agent-embed src=\"file:///<artifact_path>/widget.html\"></agent-embed>\n24:     ```\n25: \n26: ## Constraints & Theming\n27: \n28: *   **External Assets & Tailwind CSS**: All external CDNs are blocked by CSP,\n29:     except for one allowlisted gstatic Tailwind dependency that you **CAN** and\n30:     **SHOULD** use to style your artifacts. Include the following script tag in\n31:     your `<head>` to enable Tailwind:\n32: \n33:     ```html\n34:     <script src=\"https://www.gstatic.com/antigravity/web/dev/tailwindcss.min.js\"></script>\n35:     ```\n36: \n37: *   **Use Provided Theme Variables**: The iframe injects the app's semantic\n38:     design-system tokens, so widgets automatically match the host theme and the\n39:     user's custom colors. Surfaces (`--background`, `--content`, `--card`,\n40:     `--sidebar`), borders (`--border`), text (`--foreground`,\n41:     `--muted-foreground`, `--placeholder`), and accents\n42:     (`--primary`/`--primary-foreground`, `--secondary`/`--secondary-foreground`,\n43:     `--accent`) are all available. Typography is applied for you on the document\n44:     body — you do not need to set a font.\n45: \n46: *   **Text & Surface Colors**: Use semantic variables (`bg-[var(--card)]`,\n47:     `text-[var(--foreground)]`, `text-[var(--muted-foreground)]`)\n48:     instead of hardcoded dark/light utility classes (e.g., `bg-slate-900`,\n49:     `text-white`) to ensure high contrast across both light and dark themes.\n50: \n51: *   **Do Not Declare Local Fallbacks on `:root`**: Never define local color\n52:     fallbacks on `:root` in a `<style>` block; the host environment manages\n53:     theme variables dynamically.\n54: \n55: *   **HTML Boilerplate Template**: Recommended base template:\n56: \n57:     ```html\n58:     <!DOCTYPE html>\n59:     <html>\n60:     <head>\n61:       <script src=\"https://www.gstatic.com/antigravity/web/dev/tailwindcss.min.js\"></script>\n62:     </head>\n63:     <body class=\"bg-transparent text-[var(--foreground)] antialiased p-5\">\n64:       <div class=\"bg-[var(--card)] text-[var(--foreground)] border border-[var(--border)] rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm\">\n65:         <h2 class=\"text-[var(--foreground)] font-semibold text-lg\">Title</h2>\n66:         <p class=\"text-[var(--muted-foreground)] text-sm\">Description</p>\n67:         <!-- Interactive content goes here -->\n68:       </div>\n69:     </body>\n70:     </html>\n71:     ```\n72: \n73: *   **General styling**: Aim for a clean, premium aesthetic. For `<canvas>`,\n74:     check `document.documentElement.classList.contains('light')` to adapt\n75:     colors.\n76: \n77: ## Deciding on Placement (Inline vs. Standalone)\n78: \n79: **Default to artifact only** — reference the HTML artifact in your response and\n80: let the user open it in the side pane. Consider inlining when the widget is\n81: compact (comfortably under 500px tall) and directly illustrates the surrounding\n82: explanation (e.g., a small educational widget, plot, or diagram). Larger, more\n83: complex content (data dashboards, simulations, app prototypes) should stay\n84: artifact-only. Always follow the user's explicit preference if stated.\n85: \n86: ## Designing Inline Widgets (Cards & Transparency)\n87: \n88: When embedding inline in chat (`<agent-embed>`), style widgets as native chat\n89: components:\n90: \n91: *   **Transparent Root Background**: Always set `<body class=\"bg-transparent\n92:     ...\">` so the widget blends seamlessly into the chat container.\n93: *   **Card-Based Layouts**: Wrap inline content and controls in a card container\n94:     (as shown in the Boilerplate Template above) to provide elevation and\n95:     prevent loose text in light mode.\n96: *   **Standalone Artifacts**: For full-page side-pane artifacts (like\n97:     dashboards), use a solid background (e.g., `bg-[var(--background)]`).\n98: \n99: ## Sizing Inline Embeds\n100: \n101: For inline embeds, it is important to think **small and compact**.\n102: \n103: Inline embeds only have a **500px** height viewport. Past that the widget\n104: scrolls inside a small box and the user sees only a fragment of what you built,\n105: so don't build inlined widgets that are too tall.\n106: \n107: *   **Do not set a `height` attribute on `<agent-embed>`.** It is ignored.\n108: *   **Think compact** Think carefully about designing something that is compact\n109:     and fits nicely inline in the chat height budget.\n110: *   **If the idea genuinely needs more room, make it a standalone artifact.** A\n111:     scrolling inline widget is usually wrong — full-height in the side pane\n112:     beats cropped in the chat.\n113: \n114: After generating the artifact, consider whether it is sufficiently compact to be\n115: useful inline and adjust if needed.\n116: \n117: > [!IMPORTANT] Never size an inline widget relative to the viewport: no\n118: > `h-screen`, `min-h-screen`, `100vh`, or `height: 100%` on a top-level\n119: > container. The frame's viewport is derived from your content, so these feed\n120: > themselves and the widget collapses to a sliver. Use padding for breathing\n121: > room instead.\n122: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":54,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-08T07:11:27Z","thinking":"**Crafting Visualizations**\n\nI'm incredibly excited about the generative_ui skill; it allows for inline HTML embedding. I can now envision beautifully structured HTML with SVGs for all seven diagrams. These diagrams will function as \"visual anchors,\" providing a central point for user interaction.\n\n\n**Envisioning Visual Components**\n\nI'm now picturing \"prompt images\" for the exam, and I'm developing the HTML artifact, `GTU_MidSem_Diagrams.html`, with seven SVG cards. Each diagram has a unique visual representation: Pattern Allowances with different lines, Split and Match Plate Patterns, Investment Casting phases, Gas Welding Flames with distinct cones, Rolling Derivation with rolls and contact angle, and Extrusion with forward and backward scenarios.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Visual reference guide containing precise, exam-ready SVGs for the 7 required GTU mid-sem diagrams.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n  <script src=\"https://www.gstatic.com/antigravity/web/dev/tailwindcss.min.js\"></script>\n</head>\n<body class=\"bg-[var(--background)] text-[var(--foreground)] antialiased p-5\">\n  <div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-6\">\n    <div class=\"mb-8\">\n      <h1 class=\"text-2xl font-bold\">GTU Mid-Sem: Required Diagrams</h1>\n      <p class=\"text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\">Replicate these sketches exactly as shown to score full marks on 7-mark questions.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- 1. Pattern Allowances -->\n    <div class=\"bg-[var(--card)] text-[var(--foreground)] border border-[var(--border)] rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm\">\n      <h2 class=\"font-semibold text-lg mb-2\">1. Pattern Allowances (Machining & Draft)</h2>\n      <p class=\"text-[var(--muted-foreground)] text-sm mb-4\">Draw the draft angle and dotted machining lines.</p>\n      <div class=\"flex justify-center bg-white p-4 rounded-lg\">\n        <svg width=\"400\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n          <!-- Final casting shape -->\n          <rect x=\"120\" y=\"50\" width=\"160\" height=\"100\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#64748b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n          <text x=\"180\" y=\"100\" fill=\"#64748b\" font-size=\"14\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Final Casting</text>\n          \n          <!-- Pattern with draft -->\n          <polygon points=\"100,150 120,50 280,50 300,150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0f172a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n          <text x=\"310\" y=\"120\" fill=\"#0f172a\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Draft Allowance (Taper)</text>\n          \n          <!-- Machining allowance -->\n          <polygon points=\"90,160 110,40 290,40 310,160\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,5\"/>\n          <text x=\"120\" y=\"30\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Machining Allowance (Dotted)</text>\n        </svg>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- 2. Types of Patterns -->\n    <div class=\"bg-[var(--card)] text-[var(--foreground)] border border-[var(--border)] rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm\">\n      <h2 class=\"font-semibold text-lg mb-2\">2. Types of Patterns (Split & Match Plate)</h2>\n      <p class=\"text-[var(--muted-foreground)] text-sm mb-4\">Draw these rough sketches when listing pattern types.</p>\n      <div class=\"flex justify-center gap-8 bg-white p-4 rounded-lg\">\n        <!-- Split Pattern -->\n        <svg width=\"200\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n          <text x=\"60\" y=\"20\" fill=\"#0f172a\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Split Pattern</text>\n          <path d=\"M 50 100 Q 100 40 150 100 Z\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0f172a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n          <path d=\"M 50 100 Q 100 160 150 100 Z\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0f172a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n          <line x1=\"40\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4,4\"/>\n          <!-- Dowel pins -->\n          <rect x=\"70\" y=\"85\" width=\"5\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#0f172a\"/>\n          <rect x=\"125\" y=\"85\" width=\"5\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#0f172a\"/>\n          <text x=\"165\" y=\"105\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"10\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Parting Line</text>\n        </svg>\n        <!-- Match Plate -->\n        <svg width=\"200\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n          <text x=\"40\" y=\"20\" fill=\"#0f172a\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Match Plate Pattern</text>\n          <rect x=\"30\" y=\"95\" width=\"140\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#cbd5e1\" stroke=\"#0f172a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n          <path d=\"M 70 95 C 70 60 130 60 130 95\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0f172a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n          <path d=\"M 70 105 C 70 140 130 140 130 105\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0f172a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n          <text x=\"175\" y=\"105\" fill=\"#0f172a\" font-size=\"10\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Plate</text>\n        </svg>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- 3. Investment Casting -->\n    <div class=\"bg-[var(--card)] text-[var(--foreground)] border border-[var(--border)] rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm\">\n      <h2 class=\"font-semibold text-lg mb-2\">3. Investment Casting</h2>\n      <p class=\"text-[var(--muted-foreground)] text-sm mb-4\">Show the wax tree and the ceramic shell formation.</p>\n      <div class=\"flex justify-center bg-white p-4 rounded-lg\">\n        <svg width=\"500\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 500 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n          <!-- Wax Tree -->\n          <text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" fill=\"#0f172a\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">1. Wax Tree</text>\n          <rect x=\"85\" y=\"40\" width=\"10\" height=\"120\" fill=\"#fcd34d\" stroke=\"#000\"/>\n          <circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"80\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#fcd34d\" stroke=\"#000\"/>\n          <line x1=\"80\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"85\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n          <circle cx=\"115\" cy=\"110\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#fcd34d\" stroke=\"#000\"/>\n          <line x1=\"95\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"110\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n          \n          <!-- Dipping -->\n          <text x=\"210\" y=\"20\" fill=\"#0f172a\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">2. Slurry Dipping</text>\n          <path d=\"M 190 60 L 190 160 L 290 160 L 290 60\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0f172a\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n          <rect x=\"192\" y=\"100\" width=\"96\" height=\"58\" fill=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n          <!-- Tree going in -->\n          <rect x=\"235\" y=\"40\" width=\"10\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#fcd34d\" stroke=\"#000\"/>\n          <circle cx=\"215\" cy=\"120\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#fcd34d\" stroke=\"#000\"/>\n          <line x1=\"230\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"235\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n          \n          <!-- Dewaxing/Pouring -->\n          <text x=\"360\" y=\"20\" fill=\"#0f172a\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">3. Pouring into Shell</text>\n          <!-- Shell -->\n          <path d=\"M 400 40 L 400 160 M 370 80 A 15 15 0 1 0 370 110 M 430 110 A 15 15 0 1 0 430 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#cbd5e1\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n          <!-- Pouring metal -->\n          <path d=\"M 395 20 L 405 20 L 400 150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n        </svg>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- 4. Gas Welding Flames -->\n    <div class=\"bg-[var(--card)] text-[var(--foreground)] border border-[var(--border)] rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm\">\n      <h2 class=\"font-semibold text-lg mb-2\">4. Gas Welding: 3 Flames</h2>\n      <p class=\"text-[var(--muted-foreground)] text-sm mb-4\">You MUST label the zones and draw the correct proportions.</p>\n      <div class=\"flex flex-col items-center gap-4 bg-white p-4 rounded-lg\">\n        <svg width=\"400\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n          <!-- Torch tip common -->\n          <rect x=\"20\" y=\"25\" width=\"40\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n          <rect x=\"20\" y=\"95\" width=\"40\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n          <rect x=\"20\" y=\"165\" width=\"40\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n          \n          <!-- Neutral Flame -->\n          <text x=\"300\" y=\"35\" fill=\"#0f172a\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Neutral Flame</text>\n          <path d=\"M 60 25 Q 150 15 250 30 Q 150 45 60 35\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\"/>\n          <path d=\"M 60 27 Q 100 25 120 30 Q 100 35 60 33\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n          <text x=\"130\" y=\"20\" fill=\"#000\" font-size=\"10\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Inner Cone</text>\n          \n          <!-- Oxidizing Flame -->\n          <text x=\"300\" y=\"105\" fill=\"#0f172a\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Oxidizing Flame</text>\n          <path d=\"M 60 95 Q 120 85 200 100 Q 120 115 60 105\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\"/>\n          <path d=\"M 60 97 Q 80 95 90 100 Q 80 105 60 103\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n          <text x=\"100\" y=\"90\" fill=\"#000\" font-size=\"10\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Short, Pointed Cone</text>\n\n          <!-- Carburizing Flame -->\n          <text x=\"300\" y=\"175\" fill=\"#0f172a\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Carburizing Flame</text>\n          <path d=\"M 60 165 Q 160 155 280 170 Q 160 185 60 175\" fill=\"#bae6fd\" stroke=\"#0284c7\"/>\n          <path d=\"M 60 166 Q 120 160 180 170 Q 120 180 60 174\" fill=\"#7dd3fc\" stroke=\"#0284c7\"/>\n          <path d=\"M 60 168 Q 100 165 120 170 Q 100 175 60 172\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n          <text x=\"190\" y=\"195\" fill=\"#000\" font-size=\"10\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Acetylene Feather</text>\n        </svg>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- 5. Rolling Derivation -->\n    <div class=\"bg-[var(--card)] text-[var(--foreground)] border border-[var(--border)] rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm\">\n      <h2 class=\"font-semibold text-lg mb-2\">5. Rolling Derivation Geometry</h2>\n      <p class=\"text-[var(--muted-foreground)] text-sm mb-4\">Essential for deriving $l = \\sqrt{R\\Delta t}$</p>\n      <div class=\"flex justify-center bg-white p-4 rounded-lg\">\n        <svg width=\"400\" height=\"250\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 250\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n          <!-- Rolls -->\n          <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"50\" r=\"70\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#64748b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n          <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"200\" r=\"70\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#64748b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n          \n          <!-- Center points -->\n          <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"50\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#000\"/>\n          <text x=\"210\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#000\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">O</text>\n          \n    